0..65 Comment "/// This source presents the circle loop words as a rewrite type."
66..69 Comment "///"
70..114 Comment "/// `Loop` and `Unloop` are inverse letters."
115..177 Comment "/// Two cancellation rules compute each word to a normal form."
178..257 Comment "/// One stratum down, these words are the paths `Path[.A = Circle](Base, Base)`"
258..314 Comment "/// of `circle.gandr`, the HoTT book\'s circle of § 8.1."
315..318 Comment "///"
319..383 Comment "/// A fold must respect both rules before the checker admits it."
384..452 Comment "/// The winding and spinning sources map between words and integers."
453..456 Comment "///"
457..508 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/loop-winding.gandr"
509..558 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/loop-space.gandr"
